---
/**
 * oem/links <Header> — a THIN WRAPPER over the library's header.
 *
 * This file used to be a hand-rolled `<header>`: its own sticky bar, its own
 * brand markup and ~105 lines of scoped CSS. It was the LAST fork on this
 * site — the footer is already the library's `astro/Footer.astro` and all
 * fifteen `src/astro/` components are vendored — but the bar still rendered
 * `class=""`, with no `.cm-*` class anywhere, so none of the rules the
 * library owns could reach it.
 *
 * MEASURED in WebKit at 375x667 / 390x844 / 1280x900 (2026-10-09), against
 * the LIVE site and against a local build of HEAD, which agreed exactly
 * because the fork had not drifted:
 *
 *   header            class=""  — `.cm-header` never applied
 *   theme toggle      32x32     — `min-height: auto`; no tap floor at all
 *   header background rgb(10,10,10) — already fully opaque, so the
 *                                   `backdrop-filter: blur(8px)` in the old
 *                                   scoped block was inert over it
 *   GitHub link       18x18     — width came entirely from the inline SVG
 *   brand             x=20, 117.03x25.81 at 375 (300 at 1280)
 *
 * That is the whole argument for the shared component: the 44px coarse-pointer
 * tap floor, the icon link's pinned box and the scroll shadow are rules the
 * library already measured and fixed. A parallel implementation does not have
 * them, and a consumer cannot opt into a fix it does not render. `.cm-icon-btn`
 * is the one that matters on a phone: on a coarse pointer the library sizes it
 * `var(--tap)` = 44px, while a hand-rolled `.theme-toggle { width: 32px }`
 * sits outside that media query and can never be floored by it.
 *
 * What this file owns now is only this site's own decisions:
 *
 *   - the brand label, taken from `astro/config.ts` (the ONE place that sets
 *     this site's identity) rather than left to the library placeholder;
 *   - that a link page has NOWHERE to navigate. `links` is empty on purpose,
 *     and the library renders no burger and no link row when it is empty —
 *     the old file's `<!-- No nav -->` comment was a decision with no markup
 *     behind it, and now it is a decision with no markup behind it;
 *   - the GitHub glyph as an `extraLinks` entry. The library ships the mark
 *     for the well-known icon links so the two cannot be separated: it keys
 *     off `label`, and an extraLink with neither a mark nor a slot renders a
 *     zero-width, unclickable link and nothing else.
 *
 * The theme toggle is the library's `showThemeToggle` button. Both the old
 * hand-rolled one and the library's carry `data-cm-theme-toggle`, which is
 * the selector the runtime binds (cli-mono.js TOGGLE_SEL), so this migration
 * changes the box the button gets, not the wiring behind it.
 */
import Header from '../astro/Header.astro';
import { SITE } from '../astro/config';
import { AUTHOR_GITHUB } from '../consts';
---

<Header
	brand={SITE.title}
	homeHref={import.meta.env.BASE_URL}
	extraLinks={[{ href: AUTHOR_GITHUB, label: 'GitHub' }]}
/>
